          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#dagger_functors"} Dagger functors
              %li
                %a{:href => "#core_of_a_presetoid"} Core of a presetoid
              %li
                %a{:href => "#univalent_setoids"} Univalent setoids
              %li
                %a{:href => "#see_also"} See also
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In set theory, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/setoid"} setoid
            is usually described as a
            %em set
            with a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-equivalence+relation"} pseudo-equivalence relation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            or more generally in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intensional+type+theory"} intensional type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/collection"} collection
            with a pseudo-equivalence relation”. Presetoids arise from the most general possible notion of “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/collection"} collection
            with a pseudo-equivalence relation” in homotopy type theory , in the same way that the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/precategory"} precategory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pregroupoid"} pregroupoid
            arise when defining categories and groupoids.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong pseudo-equivalence relation
            on a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a family of sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(a, b)
            of
            %strong morphisms
            for each element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b:A
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                for each element
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
                a family of morphisms
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{id}(a):Hom(a, a)
            %li
              %p
                for each object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b:A
                a family of functions
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} dagger
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{dagger}(a, b):Hom(a, b) \to Hom(b, a)
            %li
              %p
                for each object
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b:A
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c:A
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} comp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{comp}(a, b, c):(Hom(a, b) \times Hom(b, c)) \to Hom(a, c)
          %p
            A
            %strong presetoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            consists of a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ob
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ob(A)
            of
            %strong objects
            and a pseudo-equivalence relation
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Hom
                    %mo ,
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                    %mo ,
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} dagger
                    %mo ,
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} comp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathrm{Hom}, \mathrm{id}, \mathrm{dagger}, \mathrm{comp})
          %h2#dagger_functors Dagger functors
          %p
            The structure-preserving maps between two presetoids are called
            = succeed "." do
              %strong dagger-functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F:A \to B
            between two presetoids
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            consists of
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a function
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi Ob
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ob
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ob
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_{Ob}:\mathrm{Ob}(A) \to \mathrm{Ob}(B)
            %li
              %p
                a family of functions
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Hom
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Hom
                        %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi Ob
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi Ob
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_{hom}(a, b):\mathrm{Hom}_A(a, b) \to \mathrm{Hom}_B(f_{Ob}(a), f_{Ob}(b))
            %li
              %p
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identifications"} identifications
                indicating that the identity morphism, dagger, and the composition operation are preserved:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} idpreserve
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi Ob
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{idpreserve}(a):f_{Hom}(a, a)(\mathrm{id}_A(a)) = \mathrm{id}_B(f_{Ob}(a))
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} daggerpreserve
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} dagger
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} dagger
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi Ob
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi Ob
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{daggerpreserve}(a, b, f):f_{Hom}(a, b)(\mathrm{dagger}_A(a, b)(f)) = \mathrm{dagger}_B(f_{Ob}(a), f_{Ob}(b))(f_{Hom}(a, b)(f))
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} comppreserve
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} comp
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} comp
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{comppreserve}(a, b, c, f, g):f_E(a, c)(\mathrm{comp}_A(f,g)) = \mathrm{comp}_B(f_{Hom}(a, b)(f), f_{Hom}(b, c)(g)
          %p
            An dagger functor between two presetoids is
            %strong faithful
            if every morphism function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Hom
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Hom
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi Ob
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi Ob
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_{Hom}(a, b):\mathrm{Hom}_A(a, b) \to \mathrm{Hom}_B(f_{Ob}(a), f_{Ob}(b))
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
            %strong embedding-on-objects
            if the object function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi V
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_V:V_A \to V_B
            is an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding"} embedding
            %strong equivalent-on-objects
            if the object function is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+homotopy+type+theory"} equivalence of types
          %h2#core_of_a_presetoid Core of a presetoid
          %p
            A subpresetoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            of a presetoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a presetoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            with an faithful embedding-on-objects dagger functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:G \to A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a subpregroupoid if the pseudo-equivalence relation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            additionally come with:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                for every object
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo :
                        %mi Ob
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:Ob(G)
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
