          %h2#univalent_setoids Univalent setoids
          %p
            There are two ways to show that two objects of a presetoid are identified with each other: by way of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pregroupoid"} pregroupoid
            of a presetoid. Univalent setoids are precisely the presetoids which the two notions of identifying objects with each other coincide.
          %p
            For each object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo :
                  %mi Ob
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:Ob(A)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo :
                  %mi Ob
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b:Ob(A)
            of a presetoid
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} idtoiso
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi A
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{idtoiso}(a, b):(a =_A b) \to (a \cong_A b)
          %p
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
            to the type of isomorphisms in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pregroupoid"} pregroupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
